  "details": "1. Create a humanoid avatar with 3 extra bones coming off of the head (i.e. to simulate a physboned ear). Add 2 extra bones coming off of the hip to simulate a tail.  Give it 7 random meshes, weightpaint and position them all to the last of the 3 extra bones. Export FBX and label it PC FBX. Dissolve the 2 tailbones together into 1 tailbone, to simulate quest optimization. Join all 7 meshes into 1 to simulate quest optimization. Export FBX and label it Quest FBX. \n\n2. Setup both avatars in unity, assign a single physbone component at the root of the 3 extra bones. setup colliders for touching and grabbing.\n\n3. Upload into VRC with PC fbx on PC side, Quest FBX on android side. \n\n4. Have one client wear it on PCVR, have another client wear it on quest. \n\n5. Touch/pat the simulated 3 bone ear on each respective platform, and observe the proper motion\n\n6. Grab the bone on each platform. Observe that translation of the bone does not follow the hand on the opposite platform. I.e. if PC grabs Quest \"ear\", quest will not see the ear follow the hand of the PC user and vice versa. If Quest grabs PC or even grabs their own \"ear\", PC will not see the \"ear\" follow the hand of the quest user's self-grab\n\nIs this expected behavior? Despite the armature being the exact same on the physbone being grabbed? As well as the physbone settings being identical? With the colliders being in the exact same places?\n\nTested on buiid:\n\nVRC Open Beta and Release as of 7/31/24",
